# CI before commit

Do not create a git commit until `npm run ci` has passed in this session against the files you are about to commit.

`npm run ci` is the local equivalent of `.github/workflows/ci.yml`:

```bash
npm run lint
npm run test
npm run typecheck
npm run build
```

- If any step fails, fix it and re-run the full `npm run ci`. Do not commit a red tree.
- Do not use `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, or otherwise skip hooks.
- The `pre-commit` hook also runs `npm run ci`. Treat a hook failure as a hard stop.
- Docs-only or config-only commits still require a green `npm run ci`.
